<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Small circular thumb for the fast scroller (see FastScrollerHelper). Replaces AndroidFastScroll's
    afs_md2_thumb, which is an 8dp x 52dp rounded rect.

    Circle geometry: radius is HALF of width/height. If you retune the size, retune the radius with it
    or it stops being round. Both dimensions must be present and non-negative - the FastScroller
    constructor range-checks thumbDrawable's intrinsic width AND height (unlike the track, which is
    checked on width only).

    12dp is wider than the 8dp track, so the thumb sits ~4dp further in from the edge than afs_md2_thumb
    did. That is fine and intentional now that the track is invisible (fast_scroll_track.xml).

    No <padding>: afs_md2_thumb carries top/bottom 4dp to inset itself inside its 52dp box, which would
    squash a circle this size.

    Tint mirrors afs_md2_thumb's ?colorControlActivated rather than a hardcoded colour. The app theme is
    Theme.Material3Expressive.DynamicColors.DayNight.NoActionBar, so that attr resolves into the dynamic
    scheme and stays correct in both light and dark. Load this via AppCompatResources.getDrawable with a
    themed (Activity) context so the attr resolves - FastScrollerHelper does.

    TOUCH TARGET IS NOT AFFECTED by shrinking this. FastScroller.isInViewTouchTarget expands every hit
    area to afs_min_touch_target_size (48dp in the AAR), so a 12dp thumb still gets a 48dp grab area.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="rectangle"
    android:tint="?attr/colorControlActivated">

    <corners android:radius="6dp" />

    <size
        android:width="12dp"
        android:height="12dp" />

    <solid android:color="@android:color/white" />

</shape>
